# Deliverables: `Tests/`, `docs/` and `scripts/` are tracked.
#
# All three were previously listed here, unanchored. An unanchored pattern
# matches at ANY depth, so `Tests/` excluded the .NET test project (333 tests)
# AND `ai/tests/` (431 tests); `scripts/` excluded the database seed and the
# skill-catalogue generator. Nothing reported this -- CI simply ran fewer tests
# and passed, which reads as success.
#
# The lines are deleted rather than anchored. Writing `/Tests/` would still
# match the real top-level `Tests/` directory and still exclude it; anchoring
# only stops a pattern from over-matching nested directories, and the fix here
# is to not exclude the deliverable at all.

# scripts/ is tracked, EXCEPT the files below.
#
# Excluded individually rather than by ignoring `scripts/` and negating the
# exceptions: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a `!` pattern
# underneath it never gets a chance to match. Excluding the six files directly
# is the only form that actually works.
#
# These six embed a development database or Redis password as a default, and a
# committed secret cannot be un-committed -- removing the file later leaves the
# blob in history. Each reads the real value from the environment; the fallback
# only exists so the script runs against a local box. Rotate the credentials and
# these can be tracked like everything else.
scripts/reset_dev_data.py
scripts/seed_fixtures.py
scripts/test_data_report.py
scripts/test_deep_workflows.py
scripts/test_workflows.py
scripts/get_otp.py

## Secrets — never commit these
# A Firebase service account grants full programmatic access to the project
# (FCM, Auth, Firestore, Storage). It is referenced by *path* from
# server/WebOfWork.Api/appsettings.Development.json and is expected to live
# OUTSIDE the repository, e.g. C:\devkeys\.
*serviceaccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
# mobile/android/app/google-services.json is deliberately NOT matched here: it is
# a public API key + app id, and the Android Gradle plugin requires it to exist.
